VulkanTron @VULKANTRON_VERSION@

Run ./bin/vulkantron --obsidian to select the Obsidian arena for this session.
Run ./bin/vulkantron to use your saved presentation. The executable finds the
included assets and shaders relative to its location, including when launched
from another working directory. Run ./bin/vulkantron --help for options.
The preserved OpenGL comparison executable is ./bin/gltron.

This @CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME@ @CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR@ build uses direct Vulkan 1.3,
SDL3 @GLTRON_SDL_VERSION@, and libpng. Audio: @GLTRON_AUDIO_DESCRIPTION@.
Install runtime libraries and your GPU's Vulkan driver through your distribution.
Drivers and system shared libraries are not bundled. --validation additionally
requires the Khronos validation layer.

Obsidian adds a dark luminous arena, newly authored cycle models and textures,
approximate floor reflections, bloom confined to each player view, original
YuE2 music, and synthesized engine/boost/impact effects. Reflections are an
artistic approximation. The original game rules, AI, controls, cameras and
local multiplayer layouts remain shared with the faithful port. Classic and
faithful artpacks, original music, and custom controls remain menu selections.
The --obsidian session choice is saved only when you save preferences.

Default first-player controls: A/S turn, E boost, Q/W glance, Space pause,
Escape menus, F10 camera. Existing saved bindings take precedence. F1/F2/F3/F4
select single/stacked/four-player/automatic views.
VulkanTron preferences default to $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vulkantron/.gltronrc, or
~/.config/vulkantron/.gltronrc. Screenshots default to
$XDG_STATE_HOME/vulkantron/screenshots, or ~/.local/state/vulkantron/screenshots.
VULKANTRON_CONFIG_DIR and VULKANTRON_SCREENSHOT_DIR override those directories.
F5 saves preferences; F11 saves BMP; F12 saves PNG. When installing through
tools/install_vulkantron_launcher.py, a fresh app profile selects Obsidian.
The optional --select-obsidian installer flag backs up an existing VulkanTron
profile and changes only its bundled artpack/music selections.

COPYING contains the game license. licenses/LUA-COPYRIGHT.txt contains the
bundled Lua notice. The included documentation records provenance, architecture,
verification results and platform limits. OBSIDIAN_AUDIO.md documents prompts,
seeds, source preservation, file checks and the absence of a listening review.
The installed YuE2 model card identifies its weights as CC BY-NC 4.0; the audio
notes record this separately from the game and original asset licenses.
This remains an independent project;
the original GLTron contributors retain their authorship and asset credits.
